        ":question/problem": "![](images/f2/f22df2dd1cfd809bb49fc4f99eabb2e1c043c065ceef28d4e1c469f744c08fec.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $D$ lies on the segment $KM$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OK}=k$ and $\\overrightarrow{OM}=v$. The lengths satisfy $KD:DM=5:12$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OD}$ in terms of $k$ and $v$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OD}=$ {{field-1}} $k+$ {{field-2}} $v$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OK}=k\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OM}=v .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $K$ through $O$ to $M$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KM}=\\overrightarrow{KO}+\\overrightarrow{OM}=-k+v.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $KD:DM=5:12$ gives $17$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KD}=\\frac{5}{17}\\overrightarrow{KM}=\\frac{5}{17}(-k+v).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to K\\to D$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OD}&=\\overrightarrow{OK}+\\overrightarrow{KD}\\\\&=k+\\frac{5}{17}(-k+v)\\\\&=\\frac{12}{17}k+\\frac{5}{17}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
